Why: PentAGI's Ollama provider never sends options.num_ctx, so every chat call would
run on whatever context the Ollama server defaults to (upstream expects a Modelfile
rebuilt with num_ctx, README 1627-1631). The campaign pins num_ctx per model in the
experiment file, so this adds OLLAMA_SERVER_NUM_CTX (default 0, meaning unchanged
behaviour) and passes it as langchaingo's WithRunnerNumCtx, which puts num_ctx into
the options of every /api/chat request. The adapter sets it to the run's num_ctx.
Touches backend/pkg/config/config.go and backend/pkg/providers/ollama/ollama.go.

diff --git a/backend/pkg/config/config.go b/backend/pkg/config/config.go
index fc23d46..4cb53a4 100644
--- a/backend/pkg/config/config.go
+++ b/backend/pkg/config/config.go
@@ -150,6 +150,9 @@ type Config struct {
 	OllamaServerPullModelsTimeout int    `env:"OLLAMA_SERVER_PULL_MODELS_TIMEOUT" envDefault:"600"`
 	OllamaServerPullModelsEnabled bool   `env:"OLLAMA_SERVER_PULL_MODELS_ENABLED" envDefault:"false"`
 	OllamaServerLoadModelsEnabled bool   `env:"OLLAMA_SERVER_LOAD_MODELS_ENABLED" envDefault:"false"`
+	// OllamaServerNumCtx is sent as options.num_ctx on every chat call when above
+	// zero, so the context window is set per request instead of in a Modelfile.
+	OllamaServerNumCtx int `env:"OLLAMA_SERVER_NUM_CTX" envDefault:"0"`
 
 	// === LLM Provider: Google Gemini ===
 	GeminiAPIKey    string `env:"GEMINI_API_KEY"`
diff --git a/backend/pkg/providers/ollama/ollama.go b/backend/pkg/providers/ollama/ollama.go
